    "description": "King's guard quarters, level 3 of 3: L2 plus flourish 3. Over budget: 548 blocks vs 350 (first build 443 vs 290). Compact stone barracks house for 8 guards (the brief's 7 x 9): mess room with long table, hearth and weapon rack below, 8 beds in two rows under the roof by a stair, a porch under the jettied plaster gable; L2 a covered guard post with its own roof, banners, rugs; L3 a drill corner with a straw dummy and target. Not yet builder-tested: brick_stairs, carved_pumpkin, red_wall_banner, stone_brick_wall, target, vine. Decoration step adds: armor_stand, banner_pattern, item_frame.",
    "changes": "Quality-check notes: L1 outside is no longer plain: open trapdoor shutters on every window, stair sills under the side windows, flower boxes with poppies under the front windows, a lantern over the door and torches on new dark oak posts in the middle of both side walls (the side walls are no longer flat), a back window with shutters and a sill; the chimney moved to x 2 and now rises 2 blocks above the roof (hearth moved with it). L2 gets a visible feature: a covered guard post at the front corner (dark oak posts, its own small gable roof, lantern on a chain, the sentry's stool, rails). L3: the drill dummy's pumpkin faces east; the chimney campfire is gone (the chimney now fills the height).",
